description: Standardized implementation pattern for auto-save functionality across the application. This ensures consistent behavior and prevents common pitfalls like ID synchronization issues after saves.

## Core Principles:
1. **Parent-Child Architecture**: Auto-save logic lives in the parent component, child components only report changes
2. **Content-Based Comparison**: Compare actual data, not IDs which may change after save
3. **Debounced Saves**: Wait 1.5 seconds after last change before saving
4. **No Blur Strategy**: Never use blur to trigger saves - it creates poor UX

## Standard Implementation:

### Parent Component (e.g., RouteBuilder):
```typescript
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { router } from '@inertiajs/react';

export default function ParentComponent() {
    const [items, setItems] = useState<Item[]>([]);
    const saveTimeoutRef = useRef<NodeJS.Timeout | null>(null);
    const previousItemsRef = useRef<Item[]>([]);
    const itemsRef = useRef<Item[]>(items);

    // Keep itemsRef synchronized
    useEffect(() => {
        itemsRef.current = items;
    }, [items]);

    // Auto-save function
    const saveItems = useCallback(async () => {
        if (!permissions.canEdit) return;

        onSaveStatusChange?.('saving');
        const itemsAtSaveTime = [...itemsRef.current];

        try {
            await router.post(route('items.save'), {
                items: itemsAtSaveTime,
                is_autosave: true,
            }, {
                preserveScroll: true,
                preserveState: true,
                only: [], // Don't reload data
                onSuccess: () => {
                    // Update reference with saved data
                    previousItemsRef.current = [...itemsAtSaveTime];
                    onSaveStatusChange?.('saved');
                }
            });
        } catch (error) {
            onSaveStatusChange?.('error');
        }
    }, [permissions.canEdit]);

    // Debounced auto-save effect
    useEffect(() => {
        if (!permissions.canEdit) return;

        // Normalize items for comparison (exclude IDs)
        const normalizeItem = (item: Item) => ({
            // Include all properties EXCEPT id
            name: item.name,
            description: item.description,
            value: item.value,
            // ... other properties
        });

        const currentNormalized = items.map(normalizeItem);
        const previousNormalized = previousItemsRef.current.map(normalizeItem);
        
        const hasChanges = JSON.stringify(currentNormalized) !== JSON.stringify(previousNormalized);

        if (!hasChanges || items.length === 0) return;

        // Clear existing timeout
        if (saveTimeoutRef.current) {
            clearTimeout(saveTimeoutRef.current);
        }

        // Set new timeout (1.5 seconds)
        saveTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
            saveItems();
        }, 1500);

        return () => {
            if (saveTimeoutRef.current) {
                clearTimeout(saveTimeoutRef.current);
            }
        };
    }, [items, permissions.canEdit]);

    // Handle child updates
    const handleItemUpdate = (itemId: string | number, updates: Partial<Item>) => {
        // Find by ID first
        let index = items.findIndex(item => String(item.id) === String(itemId));
        
        // Fallback to sequence/position if ID not found (handles post-save ID changes)
        if (index < 0 && selectedItem) {
            index = items.findIndex(item => item.sequence === selectedItem.sequence);
        }

        if (index >= 0) {
            const newItems = [...items];
            newItems[index] = { ...items[index], ...updates };
            setItems(newItems);
        }
    };

    return (
        <ChildComponent
            item={selectedItem}
            onItemUpdate={handleItemUpdate}
        />
    );
}
```

### Child Component (e.g., PropertiesPanel):
```typescript
interface Props {
    item: Item | null;
    onItemUpdate: (itemId: number, updates: Partial<Item>) => void;
}

export default function ChildComponent({ item, onItemUpdate }: Props) {
    // Simple: just call parent's update function
    const handleFieldChange = (fieldName: string, value: any) => {
        if (item) {
            onItemUpdate(item.id, { [fieldName]: value });
        }
    };

    return (
        <Input
            value={item?.name || ''}
            onChange={(e) => handleFieldChange('name', e.target.value)}
        />
    );
}
```

## Common Patterns:

### 1. Initial Load Prevention:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    if (data.items) {
        setItems(data.items);
        // Prevent auto-save on initial load
        previousItemsRef.current = data.items;
    }
}, [data.items]);
```

### 2. Status Indicators:
```typescript
type SaveStatus = 'idle' | 'saving' | 'saved' | 'error';
const [saveStatus, setSaveStatus] = useState<SaveStatus>('idle');
const [lastSavedAt, setLastSavedAt] = useState<Date | null>(null);
```

### 3. ID Synchronization After Save:
```typescript
// If backend returns new IDs, handle in onSuccess
onSuccess: (page) => {
    const updatedItems = page.props.items;
    // Update local state with new IDs if needed
    setItems(updatedItems);
    previousItemsRef.current = updatedItems;
}
```

## DO NOT:
- Use blur events to trigger saves - it creates focus issues
- Compare entire objects including IDs - they change after save
- Save on every keystroke - always debounce
- Block user input during save - use background saves
- Create save logic in child components - keep it centralized

## Edge Cases:
1. **Concurrent Edits**: Latest change wins, consider conflict resolution
2. **Network Failures**: Show error state, retry with exponential backoff
3. **Component Unmount**: Always cleanup timeouts
4. **Large Data Sets**: Consider chunking or selective field updates

## Testing Checklist:
- [ ] Auto-save triggers after 1.5 seconds of inactivity
- [ ] Multiple rapid changes only trigger one save
- [ ] Saves continue working after initial save (ID changes)
- [ ] No focus loss during typing
- [ ] Proper cleanup on unmount
- [ ] Error states handled gracefully

globs:
alwaysApply: false
